  "description": "C199.1 (reviews V07, F08, H16): each SDK string whose meaning is a key of the web catalogs (contracts/fixtures/i18n/<locale>.json). resource: the SDK's resource name; flowKey: the COPY_KEYS key a template lists, operator copy overrides and a consent row is keyed by (null when an operator cannot override it); catalogKey: the dotted catalog key the words come from, in every locale; legal: the text's legal kind (COPY_KEYS' mark for a flowKey). :openverify-sdk:generateLocaleStrings (android-i18n) writes every mapped resource, and nothing else, into the generated strings_catalog.xml of each locale folder; no hand-written file defines one (KeyMapCatalogTest). The contest words (Phase 9 K9-33, C128.7) are decision texts that no operator copy targets, so their flowKey is null; their {{host}} and {{contact}} are filled by name by the failure screen that shows them. The nativeApp keys are the native clients' own wording (Workflow 10A Stage 1a): the web words a page, the app a screen and a debugger. serverComposed (Workflow 11A; C238.3, C238.7; orchestrator decision 18): the legal copy keys whose texts the server composes into a step's client view, operator copy included (the share_consent step's); the SDK shows the served text and its digest check, so no SDK string, catalog text or drafted translation exists for them, and generateLocaleStrings never reads them. The share_consent step's screen (Workflow 11A, clients-connect; C238.7): its title, accept, decline and withdraw labels are the web's built-in share.consent.* words with flowKey null (the served text is the server's; an operator's override of these four labels is not placed on Android), and its own words (share.step.*, share.categories.*) are the web's, never drafted here.",
